WEBVTT

00:01.110 --> 00:05.780
It certainly took you a while to find me, Leafe Knights.

00:05.780 --> 00:08.880
Now, you can't stop me!

00:09.690 --> 00:10.850
Shut up!

00:14.760 --> 00:15.560
Sasame?

00:15.560 --> 00:17.030
What's the meaning of this?

00:17.030 --> 00:19.500
Takako, you can't turn back, can you?

00:20.170 --> 00:21.130
I understand.

00:22.370 --> 00:23.340
Sasame...

00:23.340 --> 00:24.320
I...

00:30.180 --> 00:33.700
I'll abandon my knighthood for you!

00:34.840 --> 00:38.110
The boundless future stretches across the skies

00:34.840 --> 00:38.110
hateshinai mirai hirogaru kono sora

00:38.110 --> 00:42.150
And I am reborn anew

00:38.110 --> 00:42.150
atarashii jibun ni umare kawaru

00:42.150 --> 00:49.170
I'll make the snow of happiness fall all over the world

00:42.150 --> 00:49.170
sekaijuu shiawase no yuki o furasete miseru yo

00:53.350 --> 00:53.550
Prétear

01:01.400 --> 01:08.310
Destiny is there to be grasped, so stretch out your hands

01:01.400 --> 01:08.310
unmei wa tsukamu mono kono te jiyuu ni nobaseba ii

01:08.310 --> 01:13.100
There is no tomorrow which has already been decided

01:08.310 --> 01:13.100
kimerareta ashita wa nai

01:15.150 --> 01:22.050
Even if you say nothing, I know our meeting that day was no coincidence

01:15.150 --> 01:22.050
damatte ite mo wakaru ano hi deai wa guuzen janai

01:22.050 --> 01:26.960
I sensed eternity in your distant gaze

01:22.050 --> 01:26.960
tooi hitomi ni eien kanjita

01:28.790 --> 01:32.660
The light of the setting sun is beautiful

01:28.790 --> 01:32.660
kurete yuku yuuhi ga kirei

01:32.660 --> 01:35.800
If the cold wind glimmers

01:32.660 --> 01:35.800
tsumetai kaze ga hikareba

01:35.800 --> 01:41.570
I can hear your voice drifting gently

01:35.800 --> 01:41.570
anata no koe sotto kikoeteru

01:41.740 --> 01:42.040
Knowing that I'm not alone in my heart

01:41.740 --> 01:46.510
kokoro no naka hitori janai koto itai hodo

01:46.510 --> 01:49.050
Warms it so much that it hurts

01:46.510 --> 01:49.050
kono mune o atsuku suru

01:49.050 --> 01:51.780
It all begins from the point of believing

01:49.050 --> 01:51.780
hajimaru ne shinjiru koto kara

01:51.780 --> 01:55.450
These feelings are proof of being alive

01:51.780 --> 01:55.450
kono kimochi ikiru akashi

01:55.450 --> 01:55.750
The endless future and the expanding skies

01:55.450 --> 01:58.660
hateshinai mirai hirogaru kono sora

01:58.660 --> 02:02.690
Allow me to be reborn anew

01:58.660 --> 02:02.690
atarashii jibun ni umare kawaru

02:02.690 --> 02:08.800
I'll make the snow of happiness fall all over the world

02:02.690 --> 02:08.800
sekaijuu shiawase no yuki o furasete miseru yo

02:08.800 --> 02:13.400
Holding hands with you

02:08.800 --> 02:15.400
sono te tsunaide

02:15.550 --> 02:18.980
The Furthest Ends of One's Emotions

02:25.660 --> 02:26.620
Sasame...

02:28.030 --> 02:30.160
I'll sever my ties with the Knights...

02:30.160 --> 02:32.390
...and swear my allegiance to the Princess of Disaster.

02:35.730 --> 02:41.640
Even if those feelings are forbidden for someone who is supposed to protect Leafe.

02:42.170 --> 02:44.510
Could you have...

02:44.510 --> 02:48.510
That's right, Hayate. I loved Takako.

02:48.510 --> 02:51.480
No, even now, I love you!

02:58.360 --> 03:00.150
But back then...

03:02.460 --> 03:05.120
You didn't have eyes for me.

03:06.360 --> 03:11.130
In order to escape from my suffering, I had to lie to myself.

03:11.800 --> 03:17.680
To think of my comrades, to abandon love, to live for the great mission...

03:17.680 --> 03:20.680
Those are things I had to tell myself.

03:20.680 --> 03:23.770
I had to believe this was the fate God had given me.

03:25.880 --> 03:29.050
But I won't believe in fate anymore.

03:30.860 --> 03:35.260
If I can have your love, I'll gladly become a demon!

03:35.260 --> 03:37.160
What are you saying, Sasame?!

03:37.630 --> 03:39.730
I'll swear it right now.

03:39.730 --> 03:43.500
I hereby dedicate my life to you and shall become a Knight of Darkness.

03:49.170 --> 03:50.140
This...

03:52.510 --> 03:54.440
This is my answer!

04:20.670 --> 04:22.010
That's the Princess of Disaster?

04:22.010 --> 04:24.770
But that lady was so nice.

04:26.410 --> 04:27.710
I was so scared.

04:27.710 --> 04:29.280
This is no time to be cringing!

04:29.280 --> 04:32.880
We have something else we need to think about instead!

04:34.590 --> 04:36.090
Sasame...

04:36.090 --> 04:37.880
This is how it should be.

04:38.790 --> 04:44.130
A Leafe Knight isn't supposed to have feelings for the Princess of Disaster,

04:44.130 --> 04:46.620
...even if he was in love with her.

04:52.970 --> 04:55.770
It's good Takako turned Sasame down.

04:55.770 --> 04:59.280
Even Sasame's had his emotional uncertainties settled.

04:59.280 --> 05:01.980
Hey, aren't you being a bit harsh here?

05:01.980 --> 05:04.020
I'm only stating the reality.

05:04.020 --> 05:05.350
Is that so?

05:07.420 --> 05:10.960
Kei, I can understand what you said, but just because he's a Knight,

05:10.960 --> 05:12.660
...just because she's the Princess of Disaster...

05:12.660 --> 05:16.260
I think there are emotions you just can't control with logic.

05:16.260 --> 05:21.270
If I really were to fall in love with someone, I don't know what would happen.

05:21.270 --> 05:25.570
I may end up not caring about what's right and what's wrong.

05:25.570 --> 05:29.670
That may be inexcusable, but...

05:29.670 --> 05:34.630
...I don't think anyone has the right to say it's wrong to fall in love.

05:36.280 --> 05:38.480
Is that wrong?

05:44.060 --> 05:45.180
Sasame...

05:48.560 --> 05:51.620
Let's leave him alone for a while, okay?

06:00.070 --> 06:01.270
<i>Le-aese!</i>

06:12.980 --> 06:14.090
All right!

06:14.090 --> 06:15.140
Our turn!

06:19.620 --> 06:22.460
This is what it's supposed to look like when completed, but...

06:22.460 --> 06:25.060
How cute!

06:25.060 --> 06:30.600
When I entered everyone's specialties into the computer, this was the design it output.

06:30.600 --> 06:34.210
That's all right! It won't be so lonely in a house like this!

06:34.210 --> 06:37.780
Hey, Mannen! I told you that's not the place to cut!

06:37.780 --> 06:39.580
Say what? So what, even here...

06:39.580 --> 06:41.080
For one thing, it's crooked.

06:41.080 --> 06:43.080
Oh, shut up.

06:43.080 --> 06:45.480
It's because of the fact that you don't fully understand...

06:45.480 --> 06:50.160
...Himeno's feelings in moving to avoid getting her family involved, that your workmanship is so lousy!

06:50.160 --> 06:51.760
This is exactly what I'm going for!

06:51.760 --> 06:53.020
<i>Oh, jeez...</i>

06:53.020 --> 06:55.460
<i>That board there looks like it's about to fall off, Go.</i>

06:55.460 --> 06:57.330
<i>Huh? Oh, damn!</i>
Maybe I'll help out with something too.

06:59.560 --> 07:01.530
Hey, what are you doing?!

07:01.530 --> 07:03.520
Isn't there something else you need to do?

07:04.570 --> 07:06.760
You should go back one more time.

07:07.570 --> 07:10.470
Yeah, you're right. I'll do that.

07:21.850 --> 07:23.350
Mom...

07:23.350 --> 07:29.120
I'm going away for a while, but I'll definitely be back, so don't worry.

07:32.160 --> 07:33.430
And? And?

07:33.430 --> 07:37.270
Well, I asked her out on a drive, so I got my license,

07:37.270 --> 07:41.110
...but when I came to my senses, I had become her personal chauffer.

07:41.110 --> 07:42.470
I see.

07:42.470 --> 07:47.610
I don't mind the romance novel contest, but please make sure no one figures out...

07:47.610 --> 07:50.280
...the characters were modeled after Mrs. Awayuki and myself.

07:50.280 --> 07:54.190
No problem! The main character's name was changed to Tanakada.

07:54.190 --> 07:56.150
Everyone will know, then!

07:56.150 --> 07:57.420
Hey, Himeno!

08:00.260 --> 08:02.280
I have a present for the two of you.

08:03.260 --> 08:04.390
This is...

08:06.900 --> 08:08.900
It's the legendary hair growth formula...

08:08.900 --> 08:12.300
...spanning four thousand years of Chinese history resurrected into our modern times!

08:12.300 --> 08:14.310
Lots & Lots of Hair

08:12.300 --> 08:14.310
It's the Lots and Lots of Hair!

08:14.310 --> 08:16.140
Hey! This is...

08:19.380 --> 08:23.940
The latest issue of Harleharle Romance Queen!

08:22.280 --> 08:23.940
Harleharle Romance Queen

08:22.280 --> 08:23.940
Love

08:24.020 --> 08:27.050
Oh, Miss? Why did you buy these presents out of the blue?

08:27.050 --> 08:28.350
What?

08:28.350 --> 08:29.550
Himeno?

08:30.860 --> 08:32.160
Could it be...

08:32.160 --> 08:35.960
Miss Himeno has been holding back deep feelings of love toward me?!

08:35.960 --> 08:38.260
No way, no way, no way, no way!

08:37.460 --> 08:38.260
I knew it.

08:55.050 --> 08:56.810
No! Who was it?

08:56.810 --> 08:59.580
Who dug this hole here?

09:06.420 --> 09:08.480
You have it so rough, don't you, Himeno?

09:12.360 --> 09:14.230
Take care, Mayune.

09:24.980 --> 09:26.580
I brought some tea!

09:26.580 --> 09:28.810
Why, thank you.

09:28.810 --> 09:31.040
This certainly doesn't happen very often.

09:33.790 --> 09:35.750
Himeno, did something happen?

09:36.050 --> 09:38.560
Oh, of course not!

09:38.560 --> 09:40.080
Here, before it gets cold.

09:40.730 --> 09:41.690
Oops!

09:42.160 --> 09:44.320
It's because you were doing something you aren't used to.

09:45.360 --> 09:49.660
Oh, my, do look at Mawata as an example and become someone who doesn't cause so much trouble.

09:51.370 --> 09:52.930
Mawata...

10:02.080 --> 10:02.950
Who is it?

10:02.950 --> 10:04.510
It's me, Himeno.

10:07.020 --> 10:11.180
Mawata, let's talk together again, just the two of us.

10:13.830 --> 10:16.520
Well, I'm leaving now.

10:18.830 --> 10:22.100
To think, I'm going to miss this house.

10:22.100 --> 10:23.830
What a strange feeling.

10:24.370 --> 10:26.870
I overdid it trying to get this place to grow on me,

10:26.870 --> 10:29.870
...or I'd get down on myself thinking it wouldn't matter if I wasn't even around.

10:29.870 --> 10:32.400
Maybe I was just stumbling by myself.

10:33.750 --> 10:37.120
This IS my home after all.

10:37.120 --> 10:40.180
I'll definitely come back to this place.

10:45.060 --> 10:46.420
This is good.

10:50.630 --> 10:53.560
You who put shadows into your heart...

10:53.560 --> 10:57.630
...are worthy of becoming the puppet of darkness which will give me power.

10:58.470 --> 11:00.230
You poor girl...

11:00.870 --> 11:04.330
Now, give your hatred to me.

11:22.160 --> 11:24.200
Why won't you accept it?

11:24.200 --> 11:27.630
What could you still be attached to in this world of people?!

11:37.980 --> 11:38.770
I see...

11:39.910 --> 11:43.400
So you love that man that much?

12:40.770 --> 12:43.760
I had the feeling if I came here, I'd be able to meet you.

12:54.520 --> 12:55.540
Me too.

13:04.060 --> 13:05.660
Wow!

13:05.660 --> 13:06.860
It's complete!

13:06.860 --> 13:09.070
Amazing, amazing!

13:09.070 --> 13:11.730
This is yours, Himeno.

13:12.800 --> 13:15.010
This is a name plate?

13:13.240 --> 13:13.970
Himeno Awayuki

13:15.010 --> 13:16.970
We made it.

13:16.970 --> 13:18.670
It's to celebrate your move.

13:21.410 --> 13:22.810
Something the matter?

13:23.550 --> 13:24.410
Nothing...

13:24.950 --> 13:27.520
I'm glad I have all of you.

13:27.520 --> 13:30.010
I may have found the confidence to live on my own.

13:31.460 --> 13:32.580
Thank you.

13:38.060 --> 13:39.160
Sasame?

13:39.160 --> 13:40.770
It's Sasame! Sasame!

13:40.770 --> 13:42.630
Sasame's back!

13:44.470 --> 13:46.870
It looks like he's sorted through his feelings.

13:46.870 --> 13:51.380
And so, the Leafe Knights have found some resolution and we're all back together again.

13:51.380 --> 13:52.240
Thank goodness!

13:52.240 --> 13:52.970
Wait!

13:55.110 --> 13:55.870
Himeno!

14:07.390 --> 14:09.660
The house we all built together...

14:09.660 --> 14:11.460
Mean, mean!

14:11.460 --> 14:13.260
What the hell are you doing, Sasame?!

14:14.600 --> 14:17.300
Answer us, Sasame! What's the meaning of this?!

14:17.300 --> 14:18.230
Sasame!

14:31.020 --> 14:32.150
The Princess of Disaster!

14:32.150 --> 14:34.050
How did she get in Leafenia?!

14:34.050 --> 14:36.610
I brought her of course.

14:38.260 --> 14:40.420
In order to prove my love.

14:43.460 --> 14:47.060
Sasame, did you think of me all that time?

14:47.060 --> 14:50.100
Yes, all that time, even now.

14:50.100 --> 14:54.670
Sasame, if that's true, give me proof of that.

14:54.670 --> 14:57.570
For my sake, Hayate...

14:58.040 --> 14:59.510
Kill Hayate!

15:01.150 --> 15:02.550
If...

15:02.550 --> 15:08.310
If you'll do that, then I can believe you.

15:12.420 --> 15:13.560
That can't be...

15:13.560 --> 15:16.760
Sasame, this is a bad joke, right?

15:16.760 --> 15:20.460
We're partners, and there's no way you can...

15:20.460 --> 15:22.870
Hayate! Fight me!

15:22.870 --> 15:23.990
I refuse.

15:24.270 --> 15:25.900
Then I guess there's no other choice.

15:35.350 --> 15:36.350
Himeno!

15:36.350 --> 15:37.470
I'm all right.

15:39.420 --> 15:40.480
Stop it!

15:41.550 --> 15:42.880
Yes, this is good!

15:48.160 --> 15:49.160
Himeno!

15:49.160 --> 15:50.860
I have to stop them.

15:50.860 --> 15:52.960
Kei, let's prét.

15:52.960 --> 15:54.470
You can't with your injuries!

15:54.470 --> 15:56.900
Relax, I'll go stop them!

15:56.900 --> 15:58.300
Us too!

15:58.300 --> 15:59.740
I won't let you.

16:11.450 --> 16:12.380
Damn!

16:13.820 --> 16:16.120
Now you can't interfere.

16:26.000 --> 16:27.660
Sasame! Come to your senses!

16:30.770 --> 16:32.760
Now, Sasame, take the sword.

16:56.260 --> 17:00.060
I'll say this. I'm here of my own free will.

17:00.060 --> 17:02.300
Hayate, fight me with everything you got.

17:02.300 --> 17:04.100
Otherwise, Himeno will...

17:07.940 --> 17:09.040
No...

17:09.040 --> 17:10.560
Why did it end up like this?

17:30.330 --> 17:31.020
Hayate!

18:03.560 --> 18:05.860
Why did you hesitate?!

18:19.340 --> 18:22.410
Tell me how you really feel.

18:22.410 --> 18:27.620
If there is a piece of your heart that is still a Leafe Knight, you can kill me.

18:29.620 --> 18:32.260
If you really do love me...

18:32.260 --> 18:33.860
If you love me...

18:33.860 --> 18:37.020
Kill Hayate!

18:49.840 --> 18:51.210
Stop, Sasame!

18:55.850 --> 18:56.640
No!

19:05.960 --> 19:07.220
Hayate!

19:10.590 --> 19:11.600
Hayate!

19:11.600 --> 19:13.560
I changed my mind.

19:13.560 --> 19:17.070
It's not fun to just kill that man.

19:17.070 --> 19:19.170
I want to make him suffer a lot more.

19:19.170 --> 19:22.800
I'll let him live until he's in such despair, he'll beg to die,

19:23.840 --> 19:26.000
...to you, who shall become my servant.

19:26.910 --> 19:28.210
Sasame...

19:28.950 --> 19:33.050
I shall grant you a new power.

19:33.050 --> 19:34.210
Now...

19:37.860 --> 19:40.650
This is the moment which I have longed for.

19:50.130 --> 19:52.340
Leafe's being drawn out?!

19:52.340 --> 19:53.270
That is...

20:04.350 --> 20:05.510
Sasame?

20:08.150 --> 20:09.550
This is...

20:11.560 --> 20:12.720
Leafenia is...

20:19.060 --> 20:21.630
Now, let's go, Sasame.

20:21.630 --> 20:24.100
You have a purpose to fulfill.

20:25.940 --> 20:29.040
Wait! Sasame, please come back!

20:29.040 --> 20:34.600
The Knight of Sound, the Sasame that you knew no longer exists.

20:43.650 --> 20:46.520
Sasame, please don't go! Please!

21:08.280 --> 21:09.250
Sasame...

21:23.330 --> 21:29.030
Staring out the window of a room with the lights off

21:23.330 --> 21:29.030
akari o keshita heya no mado kara miru

21:29.030 --> 21:33.270
The stars shine in the night sky

21:29.030 --> 21:33.270
yozora ni hoshi ga hikaru

21:33.270 --> 21:39.140
Today will definitely be a search for your constellation

21:33.270 --> 21:39.140
kyo koso anata no seiza sagashi

21:39.140 --> 21:42.010
To give you an arbitrary jinx

21:39.140 --> 21:42.010
katte na jinkusu

21:42.010 --> 21:47.990
If you find the seventh star, then it's the Lucky Star

21:42.010 --> 21:47.990
nanatsume no hoshi o mitsuketara <i>Lucky</i> <i>Star</i>

21:47.990 --> 21:51.960
Tomorrow, with a happy face

21:47.990 --> 21:51.960
ashita wa egao de

21:51.960 --> 21:58.060
I'll greet you good morning

21:51.960 --> 21:58.060
ohayoutte koe o kakete ageru wa

21:58.060 --> 22:02.370
It's a special thing you can't do anything about

21:58.060 --> 22:02.370
shikatanai tokubetsu

22:02.370 --> 22:03.730
My Sweet Heart

22:02.370 --> 22:03.730
My Sweet Heart

22:03.730 --> 22:10.040
I can't be the only one engrossed in all of this

22:03.730 --> 22:10.040
watashi bakari ga muchuu da nante masaka

22:10.040 --> 22:13.810
It just can't be, and I won't stand for it

22:10.040 --> 22:13.810
arienai yurusenai

22:13.810 --> 22:20.820
I want to see what you're feeling in your heart

22:13.810 --> 22:20.820
anata no naka no kimochi nozokitai

22:20.820 --> 22:29.160
To do it secretly, without you knowing

22:20.820 --> 22:29.160
kizukarenai you ni naisho de

22:41.110 --> 22:43.940
Hey, Sasame, what does it mean to love someone?

22:43.940 --> 22:47.540
Everyone has a different response to that question.

22:47.640 --> 22:50.180
I hope everyone has a happy answer.

22:47.640 --> 22:50.510
Eyes of Glass
